# PART 4 — THE 22 APPLICATION CATEGORIES AND DOCUMENT REQUIREMENTS

Implement the following 22 application categories. These are a project-level catalogue that separates several grouped APH routes into distinct user choices. Preserve the source mapping to APH Table 2.3 and the relevant annexures.

The requirements below are a starting checklist derived from the handbook analysis. Verify every item against the attached PDF before approving it for execution.

## Application 1: Extension of Approval (EoA) — Self-Disclosure

Source: Annexure 2, Section 2.1, and applicable Chapter I/II/VI provisions.

Checklist:
- Affidavit 2, digitally signed by the Chairman/Secretary of the Trust, Society or Company for self-financing institutions, or the authorised person for Government/Government-aided institutions.
- AICTE portal payment receipt for the relevant academic year, if any.
- Valid Occupancy Certificate, Completion Certificate, Building License or Form D, as applicable.
- Valid Structural Stability Certificate from a registered Structural Engineer when the building is more than 30 years from issue of the Completion Certificate.
- Valid Fire Safety Certificate.
- Satellite map showing geographical location of the land, including latitude and longitude at the entrance of the main building.
- Audited statement of accounts of the Trust/Society/Company for the previous year.
- For qualifying Government buildings older than 50 years where original documents cannot be submitted, the competent-authority letter described in the APH confirming that building norms are fulfilled.

Do not impose a universal Fire Safety Certificate expiry period unless an applicable authoritative source specifies it.

## Application 2: Introduction or Continuation of NRI Seats

Source: Annexure 2, Section 2.2.

Checklist:
- Trust/Society/Company resolution approving the introduction of seats for children of NRIs.
- Resolution in prescribed Format 3.
- Signature of the prescribed Chairman/Secretary.

Verify whether additional documents are required for continuation rather than introduction.

## Application 3: Diploma-to-Degree or Degree-to-Diploma Conversion

Source: Annexure 2, Section 2.3, and applicable Chapter II provisions.

Checklist:
- NOC from affiliating University/Board in Format 2.
- Trust/Society/Company resolution in Format 3 approving the applicable conversion.
- Signature of the prescribed Chairman/Secretary.
- State Government NOC where the relevant APH provision requires it before the academic session.
- Additional documents only where a verified APH clause makes them applicable.

Do not automatically require all Annexure 1 documents for this category; Annexure 2, Section 2.3 specifically states that all Annexure 1 documents apply to Change of Site/Location.

## Application 4: Change of Institution Name

Source: Annexure 2, Section 2.10, and Chapter I, Sections 1.5.4 and 1.5.5.

Checklist:
- NOC from affiliating University/Board in Format 2, or the official-sealed receipt permitted by the APH as proof of submission to the affiliating body.
- Trust/Society/Company resolution approving the institution name change in Format 3.
- Signature of the prescribed Chairman/Secretary.
- Applicable conditions under Chapter I, Sections 1.5.4 and 1.5.5.

## Application 5: Introduction of a New Programme or Level

Source: Annexure 2, Section 2.3 and the applicable Chapter II/III provisions.

Checklist:
- NOC from affiliating University/Board in Format 2.
- Trust/Society/Company resolution in Format 3 approving the proposed programme or level.
- Allocation of land, building and funds where required by the prescribed resolution.
