- Deterministic validation results.
- Missing evidence.
- Conflicting data.
- Clarification requests.
- Audit history.

The institutional dashboard should show appropriate status updates without disclosing restricted internal material.

## 10.1 Decision communication

When an authorised competent authority records and releases a decision, display the actual recorded outcome and official communication.

Support LoA, LoR and LoD as configurable decision/communication types only where their meaning and applicability are confirmed from the governing AICTE procedure.

For each released decision, show:
- Application ID and category.
- Institution name.
- Decision/communication type.
- Decision status.
- Decision date and timestamp.
- Issuing authority/committee, where disclosure is permitted.
- Official reference/communication number, if recorded.
- Detailed reason/explanation recorded by the authority.
- Conditions or undertakings, if any.
- Compliance requirements and deadlines, where prescribed.
- Appeal eligibility and applicable deadline.
- Official document/communication attachment.
- Available next actions.

Never generate a fake approval letter, rejection letter or statutory decision. A prototype-generated sample document must be visibly marked as a simulation.

Do not infer or automatically generate a decision reason from rule failures.

